ts of the inequality:\n\n\\[ 2^2 < t < 3.5^2 \\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[ 4 < t < 12.25 \\]\n\nSince \\( t \\) must be an integer, we list the integers that satisfy this inequality. The integers between 4 and 12.25 are:\n\n\\[ 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 \\]\n\nTo count these integers, we note that they form an arithmetic sequence starting from 5 and ending at 12. The number of terms in this sequence is:\n\n\\[ 12 - 5 + 1 = 8 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of integer values of \\( t \\) that satisfy the condition is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{8} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{8}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:601"}
